{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>However, on the fifteenth day.</b> Since regarding Pesach no 'rejoicing' is written, because no grain has yet been gathered, and regarding Shavuot only one 'rejoicing' is written, because the grain has been gathered but the fruits of the tree have not — but regarding Sukkot, when everything has been gathered into the house and the sins have also been forgiven on Yom HaKippurim, three 'rejoicings' are written: ושמחתם here, and ושמחת בחגך, and והיית אך שמח — one for grain, one for fruits of the tree, and one for forgiveness of sins. And thus it says: והיית אך שמח — you have nothing to occupy yourself with except rejoicing."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:25.118835637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}